course: dictionary
lesson: 11119
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «The cook fried the whiting for supper.» Fried and supper tell you whiting is food, so here it means a fish.
explain: Look at the words around the word, then swap in your meaning to check it. «Grandma mixed whiting with water and painted the fence.» You cannot paint with a fish, so whiting here must be the fine white powder called chalk.
explain: Some words sound the same but mean different things, so read carefully. In a story, a whiting can even be a talking fish. «"Will you walk a little faster?" said a whiting to a snail.» Only in a made-up story would a fish talk to a snail, so the context shows this is a playful tale.
fact: Whiting is a noun, and this dictionary gives it three meanings.
fact: «Whiting» means a small sea fish of the cod family, with white flesh, that is eaten as food.
fact: In the USA and Australia, other small white-fleshed sea fish are also called whiting.
fact: «Whiting» can also mean finely ground white chalk, used for whitewash, paint and cleaning.
exercise: «The whiting was fried and served with chips.» What is a whiting here? | *A small sea fish, eaten as food | A snail | A white powder for cleaning | A kind of boot
exercise: «Grandma mixed whiting with water to paint the fence white.» What does whiting mean here? | A hot drink | A snail | A fish from the sea | *Finely ground white chalk, used in paint
exercise: Why can the word whiting be tricky to understand? | It is a verb for swimming | It is always a fish | It has only one meaning | *It has more than one meaning, so context helps you choose
test: In the song, «"Will you walk a little faster?" said a whiting to a snail», what kind of creature is the whiting? | A snail | *A fish | A tiny bird | A powder used for cleaning
test: What is the best way to find the meaning of whiting in a new sentence? | Guess the longest meaning | Look only at the first letter | *Read the words around it and swap in your meaning | Skip the sentence and never come back
exam: Which meaning of whiting fits «The Victorian cook served whiting with its tail in its mouth»? | A type of shoe | *A fish that is cooked and eaten | Chalk for whitewash | A snail
